WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.530
A speed camera clocks a car at one instant,
and there's its speed, on the screen.

2
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.810
A reaction has a speed too: its rate.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.210
But the rate keeps changing
as the reaction goes on.

4
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.950
Divide the total change by the total
time, and all you get is an average.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.170
So how do you clock a
reaction at one instant?

6
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.130
In this mission, you'll
define the rate of reaction,

7
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.350
and follow reactions by gas
volume, by mass and by colour.

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.430
You'll read rates from graphs,

9
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.710
working through marble chips
reacting with acid, step by step.

10
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.560
Your mission: find the rate
of a reaction at one instant.
